{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: the code was compiled to SPIR-V with glslangValidator\n  optimized with spirv-opt -O (what follows is beyond that)\ncost model: gt1030\nsimplify: 76 SPIR-V instructions, 0 rewrites proved by SAT (bit-precise: equal for every input), 1 sum of products made dot products (proved by dot.c, below), 12 dead instructions removed\n  integer arithmetic cost under gt1030 (each instruction once): 24 -> 1 (-95.8%)\n  by kind:\n       1  a sum of products as one dot product          -23\n  rewrites:\n    %53 = OpIAdd %uint %47 %52\n      ->  udot4x8(%27, 0x9070503)   (a sum of products as one dot product; -23)\n      (line 7: b.d[i] = (x & 255u)*3u + ((x >> 8) & 255u)*5u + ((x >> 16) & 255u)*7u + (x >> 24)*9u;)\n  dot products (a sum of products as one instruction, laid out and proved by dot.c under gt1030):\n    %53 = OpIAdd %uint %47 %52\n      ->  udot4x8(%27, 0x9070503)   (cost 24 -> 1)\n      (line 7: b.d[i] = (x & 255u)*3u + ((x >> 8) & 255u)*5u + ((x >> 16) & 255u)*7u + (x >> 24)*9u;)\n      udot4x8 (4 x 8-bit lanes, unsigned): lane 0: (%27 & 0xff) * 3, lane 1: (%27 >> 8 & 0xff) * 5, lane 2: (%27 >> 0x10 & 0xff) * 7, lane 3: (%27 >> 0x18) * 9\n      %27 & 0xff is bits 0..7 of %27: lane 0 as it is\n      %27 >> 8 & 0xff is bits 8..15 of %27: lane 1 as it is\n      %27 >> 0x10 & 0xff is bits 16..23 of %27: lane 2 as it is\n      %27 >> 0x18 is bits 24..31 of %27: lane 3 as it is\n      udot4x8's sum is in 0..6120: it does not wrap\n      proved by SAT: 755 AIG nodes, 0 conflicts\n  proved; the operands' definitions were expanded up to 16 levels, the rest (loads, loop phis, spec constants) are free inputs\n  (nofile: simplified.spvasm, 2288 bytes, checksum 7637b5e3)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "spirv_simplify", "ucas": "use gt1030; spvsimplify nofile", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "spirv_simplify", "instructions": 76, "dead_removed": 12, "model": "gt1030", "cost_before": 24, "cost_after": 1, "assumptions": [], "rewrites": [{"from": "%53 = OpIAdd %uint %47 %52", "to": "udot4x8(%27, 0x9070503)", "why": "a sum of products as one dot product", "gain": 23, "line": 7, "proof": "dot"}], "dot_products": [{"from": "%53 = OpIAdd %uint %47 %52", "to": "udot4x8(%27, 0x9070503)", "line": 7, "cost_before": 24, "cost_after": 1, "relies_on": "udot4x8 (4 x 8-bit lanes, unsigned): lane 0: (%27 & 0xff) * 3, lane 1: (%27 >> 8 & 0xff) * 5, lane 2: (%27 >> 0x10 & 0xff) * 7, lane 3: (%27 >> 0x18) * 9\n%27 & 0xff is bits 0..7 of %27: lane 0 as it is\n%27 >> 8 & 0xff is bits 8..15 of %27: lane 1 as it is\n%27 >> 0x10 & 0xff is bits 16..23 of %27: lane 2 as it is\n%27 >> 0x18 is bits 24..31 of %27: lane 3 as it is\nudot4x8's sum is in 0..6120: it does not wrap", "proof": "proved by SAT: 755 AIG nodes, 0 conflicts"}]}, "notes": [{"kind": "info", "text": "the code was compiled to SPIR-V with glslangValidator"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "sat", "text": "each rewrite bit-blasted and proved equal for every input (refinement)"}, "files": [], "text": "  note: the code was compiled to SPIR-V with glslangValidator\n  optimized with spirv-opt -O (what follows is beyond that)\ncost model: gt1030\nsimplify: 76 SPIR-V instructions, 0 rewrites proved by SAT (bit-precise: equal for every input), 1 sum of products made dot products (proved by dot.c, below), 12 dead instructions removed\n  integer arithmetic cost under gt1030 (each instruction once): 24 -> 1 (-95.8%)\n  by kind:\n       1  a sum of products as one dot product          -23\n  rewrites:\n    %53 = OpIAdd %uint %47 %52\n      ->  udot4x8(%27, 0x9070503)   (a sum of products as one dot product; -23)\n      (line 7: b.d[i] = (x & 255u)*3u + ((x >> 8) & 255u)*5u + ((x >> 16) & 255u)*7u + (x >> 24)*9u;)\n  dot products (a sum of products as one instruction, laid out and proved by dot.c under gt1030):\n    %53 = OpIAdd %uint %47 %52\n      ->  udot4x8(%27, 0x9070503)   (cost 24 -> 1)\n      (line 7: b.d[i] = (x & 255u)*3u + ((x >> 8) & 255u)*5u + ((x >> 16) & 255u)*7u + (x >> 24)*9u;)\n      udot4x8 (4 x 8-bit lanes, unsigned): lane 0: (%27 & 0xff) * 3, lane 1: (%27 >> 8 & 0xff) * 5, lane 2: (%27 >> 0x10 & 0xff) * 7, lane 3: (%27 >> 0x18) * 9\n      %27 & 0xff is bits 0..7 of %27: lane 0 as it is\n      %27 >> 8 & 0xff is bits 8..15 of %27: lane 1 as it is\n      %27 >> 0x10 & 0xff is bits 16..23 of %27: lane 2 as it is\n      %27 >> 0x18 is bits 24..31 of %27: lane 3 as it is\n      udot4x8's sum is in 0..6120: it does not wrap\n      proved by SAT: 755 AIG nodes, 0 conflicts\n  proved; the operands' definitions were expanded up to 16 levels, the rest (loads, loop phis, spec constants) are free inputs\n  (nofile: simplified.spvasm, 2288 bytes, checksum 7637b5e3)\n"}, "isError": false}}
